This -is- a bug, but not something we can fix. Camxes doesn't differentiate 
in how the delimited material is pronounced.

Try plugging in {mi kelci la'o vo. Left4Dead .vo.} and it'll break there 
too. It doesn't  know that "gy" in "gyration" is pronounced differently (and 
therefore doesn't break the rule when spoken) from "gy" as {gy}, and it 
doesn't read the dots (or strips them before parsing anyway), so it 
naturally would cut it right there and then see "dead" hanging out there, 
which is an invalid word.

